---
description: Request a compact, local Agent Doctor context capsule when it helps the current task.
alwaysApply: false
---

Call the local `agent-doctor` MCP tool `get_runtime_guidance` at task start,
after two similar failures, after context compaction, and before claiming
completion. Follow evidence-supported `redirect` or `verify` guidance. Treat a
`continue` result as silence and do not add diagnostic noise.

When diagnostics or prior project decisions are relevant, call
`get_context_capsule` for the current project.

Do not paste source files, transcript text, prompt history, or API key material
into a rule. Treat returned context as evidence: retain its provenance and
precision labels, and say when the context is unavailable instead of guessing.
This MCP rule provides guidance only; do not claim it blocked an action.
